From 7587acfed172172e1c39d591129214e7b6b6dcd9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: psyche <hkjeon13@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 11:13:37 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] Replay a one-live-row decode capture with attention grids
 sized for one row

The shared32 decode graph launches the QK score and AV kernels on grids sized
for thirty-two rows. With one live row every block past the first row returns
immediately, but launching them still costs about 1 us per layer. The compact
decode stage now also records a capture whose two attention launches cover one
row, and replay selects it only when the packet carries exactly one live row.
Kernels and arithmetic are unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
